
	Prosody DTLS processing
secname	sort

	Create a DTLS[rx] endpoint
apifn	sm_dtlsrx_create
params	sm_dtlsrx_create_parms dtlsrxp
	The newly created DTLS[rx].
field	tSMDTLSrxId dtlsrx out
	A value obtained from
fnref	sm_open_module
	which indicates the module where the DTLS[rx] is to be allocated.
field	tSMModuleId module in
unstruct
	Allocates, on a specific module, a new DTLS[rx] to process incoming DTLS packets.
	If the call completes successfully, the parameter
ref	dtlsrx
	will be set to the identifier for that dtlsrx.
	<p>
	Requires the module
modref  dtlsrx
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error
error	ERR_SM_NO_RESOURCES - if insufficient resources exist to create the DTLS[rx]

	Configure a VMP[rx] to pass DTLS packets to a DTLS[rx]
apifn	sm_vmprx_config_dtls
params	sm_vmprx_config_dtls_parms configp
	The VMP[rx] which will received the DTLS packets.
field	tSMVMPrxId vmprx in
	The DTLS[rx] to pass the packets to. If this is <code>kSMNullDTLSrxId</code> 
	then the VMP[rx] will no longer pass on DTLS packets.
field	tSMDTLSrxId dtlsrx in
	Which port will receive the DTLS packets. When non-zero, use the RTCP port. Otherwise, the RTP port is used 
field	tSM_INT use_RTCP_port in
unstruct
	Configures a VMP[rx] to pass incoming DTLS packets to a DTLS[rx].
	<p>
	Requires the modules
modref  dtlsrx
	and
modref	vmprx
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

